Z||000000||overlord||04-19-2000||06:24 PM||||i have an audiovox rampage cd  player in my fiero right now..and was wondering if i can get a cd changer?  how do they hhook up? does the changer play the cds? any info would be great...dont know much about changers other than they hold stacks of cds...||||reg||1
Z||000001||N_Man||04-19-2000||06:53 PM||||if your deck has the hook up for a changer you can use one. It will be on the back of the deck and be a circular plug.<P>A changer holds and plays CD's, You deck will controll the unit, telling it what disk to play, what track, etc.<P>for the best results try and stay with the same brand. You said you have audiovox so get an audiovox changer. That way you will know things will work.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Homicidal||04-20-2000||01:35 AM||||I own a JVC 12 cd changer, mounted behind the seat, works great!||||reg||1
Z||000003||TOM||04-20-2000||10:51 AM||||In my mustangt I had two changers linked to one head unit Through a switch I made||||reg||1
Z||000004||Racer 1||04-20-2000||11:44 AM||||Theres two types of CD Changers.<P><B>1.</B> The type CD changer that hooks directly in the back of your head unit DIN connector plug.<P><B>2.</B> The type CD changer that works off your FM channel. It has a FM modulator that has set FM freqs so you just go to that freq and youll be able to listen to the CD changer. This type plugs inbetween the antenna input and the actual antenna plug. It will have a wired LCD screen where you can change tracks and look at what track your on.<P>||||reg||6
Z||000005||overlord||04-20-2000||07:53 PM||||thanx guys...i foundmy manual the other day...and i guess i would have to get the fm kind...no plug for a changer on the back of the unit||||reg||1
